course: dictionary
lesson: 14227
title: Narrate: telling the story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To narrate means to tell a story, saying what happens in order. The person who does this is the narrator. «Grandma narrated the tale of the lost sheep, starting with the farmer waking up early.» The word shows that Grandma told the events one after another.
explain: Narrate can also mean to speak the words that go with a film, TV programme or audiobook, explaining what we see. «The famous naturalist narrated the nature film, telling us what the lions were doing.» The voice is not in the picture; it explains what is happening.
explain: In a story, the narrator is the voice that tells it. If the narrator says I or we, it is first person. «I looked out of the window and saw the snow.» If the narrator says he, she or they, it is third person. «She looked out of the window and saw the snow.»
fact: To narrate means to tell a story, describing what happens in order.
fact: To narrate can also mean to speak the words for a film, TV programme or audiobook.
fact: The narrator is the person or voice who narrates.
fact: «Narrate» is a verb, so it changes: narrates, narrated, narrating.
fact: In first person, the narrator says I or we; in third person, the narrator says he, she or they.
exercise: «The captain narrated the story of the storm, one event after another.» What does narrated mean here? | Slept through the storm | Shouted at the crew | Painted a picture of the sea | *Told the story, describing what happened in order
exercise: Which kind of narrator is in «I looked out of the window and saw the snow.»? | No narrator at all | Third person, using he or she | Second person, using you | *First person, using I
exercise: A nature film has a voice explaining the lions. What is the voice doing? | Drawing the lions | *Narrating, explaining what we see | Singing a song | Crying
test: «Mum narrated the bedtime story, changing her voice for each character.» What does narrated mean? | Forgot the story completely | Drew pictures of the characters | *Told the story aloud, describing what happened | Read silently to herself
test: Which word shows a third-person narrator? | You | We | I | *She
exam: Which sentence is written in first person? | «He is reading a book.» | «She ran to the shop.» | *«I ran to the shop with my brother.» | «They walked to school together.»
